{"annotationDigest":"sha256:cc29ff577ca7fca4aecae6caa2f37f62a3a88b0f94fc4fddefd4a1d766ce5069","annotationId":"rann-358728e723ba211f968d198960a626c6","author":{"agent":"claude-code","kind":"ai","model":"claude-opus-5.5"},"createdAt":"2026-10-04T23:01:46Z","disclaimer":"AI-generated review opinion derived from the evidence package. It is not a verdict, does not change readiness, and must be confirmed by a human reviewer.","disclosureCheck":{"blocking":6,"contradictions":[],"disclosures":8,"nextDecision":"human_judgement","readiness":"not_assessed"},"findings":[{"claim":{"params":{"relatesTo":["shell/plugins/menu/MenuModel.js:stripJsonc","SW-REQ-260922-E4J2"],"scenario":"a user menu JSONC loaded via Menu.qml FileView whose second line is a // comment indented with U+00A0 (or U+3000, VT, FF, U+2028, U+FEFF): at base parseMenuJsonc returns every entry; at head it returns [] and logs 'MenuModel: failed to parse menu JSONC'"},"type":"behavior_hazard"},"detail":"This compatibility change is NOT intended: it is a regression the PR introduces. The auditor note on cf-39627352fe66ab9c records it as not intended (a note, not a decision); I re-checked that on this package. The removed regex `^\\s*\\/\\/[^\\n]*(\\n|$)` (m flag) deleted ANY JS whitespace in front of a whole-line comment; JS `\\s` includes VT, FF, U+00A0, U+1680, U+2000-U+200A, U+2028, U+2029, U+202F, U+205F, U+3000 and U+FEFF. The new scanner (MenuModel.js:25) drops only the `//...` text and copies the indent; JSON.parse accepts only space, tab, LF and CR, so the parse fails, the catch returns [] and the new console.warn fires. I ran the base (quattro-proof 1e433732) and head MenuModel.js in node on `{\\n<ch><ch>// note\\n \"a\":..., \"b\":...}`: base 2 rows, head 0 rows for VT, FF, NBSP, U+1680, U+2000, U+200A, U+2028, U+2029, U+202F, U+205F, U+3000 and U+FEFF; space and tab give 2 rows at both. The green tripwire test 'KI-MENU-JSONC-COMMENT-INDENT-WHITESPACE tripwire' (menumodel-replay.test.mjs:1058, menu-node suite, in the combined JUnit report) passes on a copy of this tree for all 21 characters against an ASCII-indented control; with the base MenuModel.js swapped in it fails. It breaks SW-REQ-260922-E4J2 on this input partition. Quickshell's FileView drops a LEADING BOM (KI text; Quickshell 0.3.1), so only a BOM at file start is masked; the same characters on any later comment line trigger it. An earlier check in a running Quickshell 0.3.1 with head 913e112d on an older upstream base showed 0 user rows for an NBSP- or BOM-indented comment line mid-file (not re-run on this tree). Fix (KI remediation, as #13968 b2dae8db does): copy any JS whitespace outside a string as one ASCII space, keep LF. Settle with the suggested test.","refs":[{"id":"shell/plugins/menu/MenuModel.js","kind":"file","line":25},{"id":"test/node/menumodel-replay.test.mjs","kind":"file","line":1058},{"id":"proof/known-issues/KI-MENU-JSONC-COMMENT-INDENT-WHITESPACE.yaml","kind":"file","line":1},{"id":"SW-REQ-260922-E4J2","kind":"requirement"},{"id":"review.compat","kind":"check"}],"severity":"high","title":"Regression (cf-39627352fe66ab9c, KI-MENU-JSONC-COMMENT-INDENT-WHITESPACE): a whole-line comment indented with non-JSON JS whitespace now empties the whole menu file","verification":{"evidence":[],"method":"behavior hazard: settled only by a recorded test outcome","note":"A runtime-behavior question the package's static facts cannot settle; it needs a test. Suggested test: \"Comment-lines-only Unicode indent partition (E4J2 input_domain)\".","status":"needs_test"}},{"claim":{"params":{"requirement":"SW-REQ-260922-E4J2"},"type":"requirement_affected"},"detail":"Function-level trace on stripJsonc (MenuModel.js:8-35) and parseMenuJsonc. The scanner widens comment stripping from whole-line comments to any `//` outside a JSON string, honouring `\\\"` escapes. E4J2's input_domain witness for comment indentation (menu-test.sh:273-285) was turned on this mirror from a nominal witness into the regression's tripw