e for the new branches is node (menu-test.sh, replay tests). The menu-live acceptance test loads a user extension with a full-line comment and trailing commas through Menu.qml's FileView in a headless sway (menu-acceptance-test.sh:172), so the scanner runs under QV4 on that shape; no live test loads an inline comment tail or a malformed file, so the new branch and the console.warn are not observed in the shell.","refs":[{"id":"shell/plugins/menu/Menu.qml","kind":"file","line":1045},{"id":"test/shell.d/menu-acceptance-test.sh","kind":"file","line":172},{"id":"SW-REQ-260922-3T3F","kind":"requirement"}],"severity":"low","title":"Question: do the scanner and console.warn behave the same under Quickshell's QV4 engine as under node?","verification":{"evidence":[],"method":"behavior hazard: settled only by a recorded test outcome","note":"A runtime-behavior question the package's static facts cannot settle; it needs a test. Suggested test: \"Live QV4 witness: inline-comment and malformed user extension in the menu-live suite\".","status":"needs_test"}}],"packageDigest":"sha256:7ec985a58e2db8055ea503bb0b3ce4c09d0242888de1dbce52e14705da0422db","packageIdentity":"epkg-9d30a2222cfc5e8c6fd171ab8c9e260339583caa606c48f34347adb81f4ac47c","riskAssessment":{"level":"medium","rationale":"The purpose is fixed and exercised, but the PR introduces a recorded regression (a comment line indented with non-JSON whitespace empties the whole menu file) that the differential harness missed; six compatibility changes await a reviewer."},"schemaVersion":"reqproof.review-annotation.v1","suggestedTests":[{"forClaim":0,"rationale":"Pins the old regex behaviour: for each JS \\s character outside JSON whitespace, a file whose (non-first) comment line is indented with it must parse like the ASCII-indented control. Fails at head today; restore the baseline witness at menu-test.sh:279 once fixed, and add the mode to the bdiff data generator.","refs":[{"id":"test/node/menumodel-replay.test.mjs","kind":"f